# Split from server.lang - dialogue bundle (aetherhaven_dialogue_merchant)
# Full translation keys are aetherhaven_dialogue_merchant.<lineKey> (see Hytale I18nModule).
aetherhaven.dialogue.merchant.appraiseJewelry=Appraise jewelry (10 gold each)
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.rep_reward_100.speaker=Vex Sunderlane
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.rep_reward_50.speaker=Vex Sunderlane
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.root.body=Vex Sunderlane. I sell the finest goods money can buy, and I keep an honest ledger. We'll be fast friends if you have coin to spend.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.root.c0=Browse your wares (gold coins).
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.root.c2=You mentioned wanting a house.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.root.c3=Your name is on the registry of a new house. You can move in whenever you're ready.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.root.c4=Your house is still waiting in the queue.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.root.c5=It is good to see you trading here today.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.root.c6=The stall is up. Come take a look.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.root.c7=About the stall build...
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.root.c8=You asked me to find space for a stall.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.root.c9=Keep your purse strings tight.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.root.speaker=Vex Sunderlane
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_abandoned.body=Fair enough. If you change your mind, the offer remains open on the table.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_abandoned.c0=Thanks for understanding.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_abandoned.speaker=Vex Sunderlane
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_accepted.body=I will camp at Corin's until the stall is standing. It is safer than a ditch, and the soup is certainly better than nothing.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_accepted.c0=See you when it is up.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_accepted.speaker=Vex Sunderlane
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_building.body=When the stall is built, I will head over and open shop. Come find me there, and we will wrap up this chapter of our agreement.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_building.c0=I need to drop the quest.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_building.c1=I will keep working on it.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_building.speaker=Vex Sunderlane
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_done.body=The stall looks honest enough. Trade may be thin at first, but once we get more visitors, business will pick up.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_done.c0=Here's to business.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_done.speaker=Vex Sunderlane
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_house_accepted.body=When the house is built, register me on the bookshelf and then come find me.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_house_accepted.c0=I'll get it done.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_house_accepted.speaker=Vex Sunderlane
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_house_finish.body=Perfect. A door that knows my knock. The only thing better is a full cashbox.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_house_finish.c0=Enjoy it.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_house_finish.speaker=Vex Sunderlane
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_house_offer.body=Stock belongs on shelves, and my boots belong somewhere dry. Stake the same house token as the rest of the town, and register me on the bookshelf when it's ready.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_house_offer.c0=I'll stake a house plot for you.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_house_offer.c1=Another time.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_house_offer.speaker=Vex Sunderlane
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_house_remind.body=Houses sometimes take seasons to finish. Complete it, register me, and come back so we can balance the ledger properly.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_house_remind.c0=I'll come back when it's done.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_house_remind.speaker=Vex Sunderlane
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_quest_stall.body=I need a place to set up my wares. Take this plot token and find a spot. The materials are your concern; I will run the counter once the work is done.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_quest_stall.c0=I'll build it.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_quest_stall.c1=Not right now.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.vex_quest_stall.speaker=Vex Sunderlane
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.gift.love=Exquisite. You have impeccable taste, and perfect timing.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.gift.like=I can move that easily. More gold for my coffers and the town treasury. It's a win-win.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.gift.neutral=It has trade value. Someone will be convinced to buy it.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.gift.dislike=I sell goods with stories, not clutter. Find a bin for that, not a stall.

aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.main_hub.fallback=If you came for the stall, updates on the ledger, or a fair trade, I am listening.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.main_hub.greeting.0=My wares are being sold and my ledger balanced. It's a good day.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.main_hub.greeting.1=I counted the coin twice this morning and everything balanced out. I almost didn't believe it.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.main_hub.greeting.2=It's easier to sell something that has a story behind it. People love the idea of having something unique to show off to others.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.main_hub.greeting.3=If you run your own shop, here's some advice: Always make your products sound better than they really are.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.main_hub.greeting.4=A little polish goes a long way when trying to barter junk off to gullible travelers.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.main_hub.greeting.5=I always make time for my favorite customer. Need anything in particular?
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.main_hub.greeting.6=I do sometimes get rare goods, but I don't take reservations. It's up to you to come by to see what I have in stock.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.main_hub.greeting.7=The ledger is caught up. Looks like I'll have some extra coins by nightfall.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.main_hub.greeting.8=I'm more likely to pay attention if you buy something first. Paying customers get my attention first.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.main_hub.greeting.9=I once sold a sword to someone because I said it was used to slay a dragon. They didn't realize I had four more just like it in the back room.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.main_hub.hint.love.0=Gemstones are always in high demand and I certainly wouldn't say no to some if you have any.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.main_hub.hint.love.1=Mastercrafted jewelry has a story to tell and I respect that.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.main_hub.hint.love.2=Rare materials make my day feel shorter and more profitable.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.main_hub.hint.love.3=A neat stack of honest currency is its own kind of flattery.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.main_hub.hint.love.4=I always appreciate it when folks deliver goods to replenish my stock.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.main_hub.hint.dislike.0=Do not try to trade me junk ore as if it were a secret treasure. I know the difference.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.main_hub.hint.dislike.1=Someone tried giving me a skull the other day. Do I look like a graverobber?
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.main_hub.hint.dislike.2=I don't trade in swamp filth. I don't want it anywhere near my shop.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.main_hub.hint.dislike.3=Broken rubbish with no market value only eats shelf space I cannot afford to waste.
aetherhaven.dialogue.aetherhaven_merchant.main_hub.hint.dislike.4=I sell goods, not compost. Rot belongs in a pile far away from my counter.